    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 14,
        "line": 4,
        "text": "You look nice, Wanda. Wanda Looks Ups pleased, and walks over to the bar. . ; WANDA You say nice things, Boris. _. BORTS . Nicesse : Wanda grins at him. Now the door to the alley opens ; and Gruska comes in, carrying a bag of coal."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 13,
        "line": 240,
        "text": "The Judge was a wonderful man.. He did intend to get the boys a new trial -- you have my word. | . Then shortly after, he died...rest his soul...before he could do any- , thing about it."
      }
